ealized they needed to add  specific testing requirements  like heavy metals microbials mycotoxins  thc potency  and a few others along with requiring  iso iec  17025 accreditation  the iso iec 7225  17025 standard is also easier to follow  considering  many other industries use this standard  you used to be able to get a license  before accreditation now you must get  accredited to get a state license  there are pros to cons there are both  pros and cons to this  a pro for requiring accreditation before  testing  or receiving a license is that  laboratories are being assessed  and being deemed competent before  testing customer samples  some cons for requiring accreditation  before testing  or receiving a license is cost most labs  do not have revenue before  they start testing so this is a big  upfront cost  assessors are not viewing any customer  generated data such as cfas  since the laboratory is not actually  testing also the validations are not  done with  in-matrix samples which could affect  results  states tend to evolve testing  requirements when they notice public  health trends such as recalls and  illnesses  for example in 2019 states started  noticing that there were an increased  number of people having respiratory  complications  due to vaping after further  investigation they later found that  vitamin e acetate was being used to cut  vaping products  this test is now required testing in  both maryland and michigan  as for recalls this could happen if some  someone found mold or foreign matter  in a product that has already gone to  shelf  some states in some states products are  also required to be  tested after they have been packaged and  are already ready to purchase  this is due to contaminants such as  microbials growing on  the product due to poor packaging or  storing oklahoma is just one state  adopting the system  several other states have revised their  testing requirements  in the past couple of years to require  additional testing  california expanded the panel of  required tests three times in 2018 alone  the in colorado now requires heavy  metals pesticides  and microbials to be tested  okay so now i'm going to move on from  cannabis to the usda  hemp final rule so what prompted the  usda to get involved  in the united states the usda regulates  agricultural exports  and goods which now includes hemp hemp  is now being cultivated for many  purposes  in the u.s including manufacturing  manufacturing cbd and cbg products  some of the primary decisions made in  this rule include dea certification  this requirement means that all hemp  testing labs must be registered with the  dea to test hemp  labs have until december 31 2022 to get  registered  this requirement is still unclear as  some labs that are testing marijuana  were previously dea registered  additional guidance is needed for labs  that are testing both hemp and marijuana  as it is likely that they will need to  pick one  the final rule establishes performance  bait  establishes performance-based sampling  requirements states are given  flexibility  to achieve performance objectives that  they desire  such as a reliability of 95 percent  some states do require licensing and iso  accreditation for hemp testing  and sampling one state that does this is  colorado  samples must be collected by usda  approved sampling agent the usda will  provide a list of authorized sampling  agents on their website  sampling agents must be trained under  the applicable usda or state training  procedures  the requirements for testing total thd  instead of  limiting the testing to delta 9 thd has  also not been changed  laboratories should meet the aoac  international standard  method performance requirements for  selecting an appropriate method  to determine mu they encourage states  to monitor review and evaluate mu  determine trends and outliers which may  indicate  quote unquote lab shopping for higher  emus  why is mu important a sample could be  borderline pass fail and mu could help  determine if a sample  needs to be retested or not usda is not  adopting requirements that hemp testing  laboratories must be approved under a  usda laboratory approval program  or undergo iso accreditation state plans  are free to include  additional requirements for hemp testing  laboratories including iso accreditation  or other certifications this decision  was largely based on cost  to recap the u.s is slowly but surely  making progress in legalization  and regulation of cannabis testing  although many states have pushed  cannabis  initiatives to a later date it still  looks promising for the future
 

